  "nativeInstructionCount": 631,
  "result": "no_new_exact_child_role_or_physical_brake_join; host_address_preservation_boundary_extended",
  "newFindings": [
    {
      "claim": "Extended prior queue-level trace through full MCU wrapper 1A5578..1A56D0 and lower tx-buffer writer 1C4666..1C486E. Selector 0 uses numeric tx handle 2 and preserves supplied low 11-bit arbitration ID.",
      "evidence": "mcu-ranges.json/can-transmit-wrapper and can-transmit-buffer-writer; checked against pinned original MCU bytes.",
      "implication": "At this traced host-MCU encoding boundary, 7E5 and 782 remain distinct addresses. The host does not rewrite either into the other here. A downstream gateway mapping or two endpoints implemented by one physical controller remain possible."
    },
    {
      "claim": "Two remaining INS code DIDs are reused in other factory namespaces: F394 at INS 723 and ERP 596; F494 at INS 723 and TRCAAL 720.",
      "implication": "DID alone is not a component-role key; route plus DID plus applicable exact identity is required. These collisions do not resolve INS MCU/audio."
    }
  ],
  "retainedFindings": [
    "All nine named subroles remain unbound. Cached full code, route and DID stay together; suffixes, numerical order and catalog name pools are not a joining rule.",
    "Eight previously observed child software identities remain parent-reported identities behind four logical CAN parents. They add no new CAN address and qualify neither physical child-unit boundaries nor separate DTC memories.",
    "782 retains ESP_BOSCH/IPB_BOSCH/BSC_BYD candidate aliases and exact code 32330011DF0B000101. OBD 7E5 retains CALID 4000825042253153 and BSCM-BrakeSystem name. There is no common exact identity across the two formats."
  ],
  "nextNarrowObservation": [
    {
      "gap": "INS MCU/audio; FRL left/right/environment; CDC/ZCU switch",
      "needed": "An applicable supplier/scanner definition or existing component record explicitly joining exact parent route+child DID/full software code with descriptive role. Re-reading same child code or hardware version does not close absent name join.",
      "vehicleRequestQualifiedByThisReport": false
    },
    {
      "gap": "Whether 7E5 and 782 are interfaces of one physical brake unit",
      "needed": "A software/hardware-applicable routing definition explicitly mapping both addresses to one component, or a documented common unique physical-unit identifier available through both interfaces. Shared role/version/CALID prefixes and pairs of zero-DTC replies cannot establish this.",
      "vehicleRequestQualifiedByThisReport": false
    }
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Owner-supplied MCU package is pinned; no installed MCU hash was obtained. Saved historical live transcripts are rechecked, not refreshed.",
    "Lower-layer result is static tx-ID encoding evidence for explicitly traced generic nonself path. It is not a new bus capture, wiring map, physical channel label or execution acceptance.",
    "Numeric tx handle 2 and frame selector 0 are implementation indexes, not physical network names. Flag bits are retained without assigning undocumented hardware meanings.",
    "No global absence claim is made for dictionaries or role definitions. Unexamined images, compressed regions and downstream gateways stay outside this bounded continuation.",
    "Frozen corpus index documents lookup provenance only; checker does not depend on mutable live index or previous reports whose historical index drifted.",
    "No new service/DID request, product allowlist change, physical unit count or child DTC-memory support is qualified."
  ],
